WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.700
Good morning John; I'm in Seattle and if you
don't believe me, there's a Space Needle out

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:10.740
the window. Come on camera. Why does it just
look white? Why is it, oop, there ya go! There

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.519
ya go, there's a Space Needle.

00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:17.529
Now you have to adjust to me again, but that
took no time at all. What? Strange camera,

00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:20.600
I do not understand you. On my last video
there was somebody who was like "Hank you

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.279
need to set your aperture settings to different
ones so that you are less blurry when you

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:29.970
move in and away from the camera!" and I said
"Oh I shall do that!" and then I did try.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.570
I couldn't find the settings.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:35.900
I am currently on a tiny mini tour of the
Pacific Northwest with Paul and Storm (Storm:

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:43.480
"I can talk to a camera and drive at the same
time, which can be amusing. Paul is not driving,

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.520
which is amusing as well." Paul: "I am not
driving. Do you find me amusing?") and Mike

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:53.130
Phirman (Mike: "Excuse me I'm just adjusting
my nutsack. What! Haha it's a pun and a prop!").

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:59.140
During the sound-check for me, which, I know
now because I am a muu-musician, professionally,

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.399
you get up on stage and you play the guitar
and you sing a song and I was singing "I'm

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:03.399
Gonna Kill You".

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:07.630
"I'm gonna kill you and all your loud ass
friends too!" And so they apparently need

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:10.680
a lot of sound check, usually its just like
duh-duh-duh-duh, sing-sing-sing-sing, and

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:14.140
it's over, but they're pretty pro at the place
we were at last night. And when I say last

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:18.369
night I mean two nights ago if you're watching
this on Friday. And Jason Finn, who is the

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:21.911
drummer for "The Presidents of the United
States of America" which is a band that I

00:01:21.911 --> 00:01:26.980
totally geeked out about when I was in high
school, starts playing the drums to "I'm Gonna

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:32.240
Kill You" and I'm like, "Oh god Hank! Don't
screw up! Stay at the same tempo, please don't

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.350
mess up; he's playing along, just play! Just
play!" And then Paul of "Paul and Storm" is

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:40.909
like "This is pretty easy, it's just the same
three chords over and over again" and he starts

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:45.130
playin' it on the piano! And I'm like "Okay!
Sound-check has turned into dreams coming

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.149
true! Excellent!"

00:01:46.149 --> 00:01:50.409
So now it is Thursday; I'm doing this video
today because this Friday is another show

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:57.450
day in Portland, Oregon! Are you from Portland,
Oregon? Are you not going to be at my show?

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.469
That is ridiculous! (Paul: "Links are in the
Doobly-Doo.")

00:01:59.469 --> 00:02:04.830
John, I'll be honest with you for a second,
I am ashamed that I make money from advertising

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:08.910
because I believe that advertising is a little
bit evil. It feels that often, advertising

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:12.820
is there to, uh, lie to us and make us do
things that we otherwise would not. But it's

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.540
not to say that I think all advertising is
bad; I mean sometimes we should do things

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.580
that we don't want to do, and sometimes its
just about making us spend money on one thing

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:21.280
instead of another thing. Yeaghaghagh, I'm
sure it's not all evil.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:24.420
I apologize to the people of Nerdfighteria,
but I am not going to turn off advertisements

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:27.710
on these videos because otherwise, I could
not make these videos. And I believe that

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:32.410
the good entertainment of these videos is
outweighing whatever damage the advertiser

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:36.721
is doing to your brain. And to my brain of
course, I also see Geico offering me up to

00:02:36.721 --> 00:02:44.080
15% or more off on my car insurance. Up to
15% or more! Up to! 15%! Or more! You could

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.420
not create a more non-specific statement!

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:49.340
And then there's these new Toyota commercials
- I believe that these are very evil - in

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.830
which this ridiculous looking child is making
his dad feel guilty about having an old car.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:58.730
The kid is like "I can't believe I have to
be seen in such an ugly thing!" Was that over

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:01.900
the top? Was that - I think that was over
the top. The moral of the story of course

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:07.560
being you, as a father, should be ashamed
for being poor and/or being fiscally responsible.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:12.640
Y'know what Toyota? Eat it! And I'm pointing
to a corndog, it's, it's just off frame. Okay

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.070
I'm feeling a little bit better now,you're
seeing advertisements, but I'm making fun

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.450
of advertisements too, so it's cool!

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:19.120
So I hope that you enjoyed this video of me
rambling on the floor of a hotel; I am in

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.670
fact on the floor. Here I am. I'm on the floor,
hello.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:25.310
People of Portland, I will see you on Friday.
John, I will see you on Monday!

